Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 08:00:00 +0800
Subject: [RFC PATCH 2/2] meta: test written-chunk idle compaction

Verify that overwritten history below the normal write-side compaction
threshold can be reclaimed after writes stop, without additional file
reads or manual compaction, while preserving current file contents.

Cover concurrent writes, compaction failures and retries, session
cancellation, and bounded tracking. Also check that non-overlapping
data does not cause unnecessary compaction.

Add an object-level test using SQLite metadata, in-memory storage and
the real vfs.Compact path. It waits for automatic compaction before
checking content, CRC and deletion of old objects. The same test can
run on unmodified upstream as a negative control.

Base: JuiceFS v1.4.1 (0b90c7db5a929ae6adc5faad948d108efd2c99f9)

Assisted-by: gpt 6
Signed-off-by: Li Lingfeng <a1151488180@gmail.com>
